@tradition midtour
// Midtour: day 182, half the year (a Sunday, Greening's last day). In the bow lounge crew write a letter to
// themselves; Oduya seals them, and Year's end (day 364) gives them back. The player's letter comes back by Mail then.
// (Letters evening, the weekly Sunday slot it once shared, was scratched in 0.62.0.)
// Design note: plans/trad-notes-seasons.md.
k: 478
title: Midtour
when: year day 182
at: 20:00-21:00
min: 25
prio: 2
jitter: 10
where: 3 room Bow lounge: lounge-seat
where: 3 room Mess hall: mess-seat
hold: none
who: oduya always, calls-home 70%, quiet-corner 65%, everyone 50%
anim: read
host: oduya
from: oduya
invite: host=oduya odds=20% line="Midtour tonight. Write to the you of six months from now. I'll keep it safe."

== mail
- Tomorrow is half the year. Midtour, {time}, in the bow lounge: write a letter to yourself. I'll seal them, and you'll get yours back at Year's end.

== ask
- Midtour tonight. I never know what to write until I start.
- Half the year gone. Are you writing a letter tonight?
- Midtour letters at eight. I'm going to tell myself to drink more water.   #funny

== here
- Don't read over my shoulder. It's for future me.   #funny
- Six months. Say something kind to yourself.   #warm
- I read last year's letter back. I was worried about things that never happened.   #warm

== thanks
- You write a letter to yourself and fold it into an envelope. Oduya seals it with a smile.   #warm

== chatter
- What did you write for Midtour? No, don't tell me. That's the rule.
- My Midtour letter last year was one line long. It was a good line.   #funny
- Oduya keeps the Midtour letters in a box nobody's allowed to touch.
